1. Upstream: this project is a derivative of rigaya's NVEnc
===============================================================================

Everything under RtgmDif/NVEnc/ originates from NVEnc, the NVIDIA encoder front
end by rigaya:

    https://github.com/rigaya/NVEnc

That project is distributed under the MIT License, and its copyright notice and
permission text are kept verbatim at the top of every file taken from it, in the
form:

    // QSVEnc/NVEnc by rigaya
    // The MIT License
    // Copyright (c) 2011-2016 rigaya

No upstream copyright notice has been removed or altered, and this project is
released under the same MIT License as upstream. That is a choice rather than a
constraint - MIT would also have permitted a copyleft release of the whole work,
but matching upstream keeps the terms uniform across the tree and is the
simplest thing to explain to anyone reusing it.

For the files listed in section 3 the upstream MIT notice is not the whole
story, because they were modified.

The RTGMC deinterlacing filter at the centre of this project - the
NVEncFilterRtgmc*.cu/.h family and the NVEncFilterRtgmcShimmerRepair* files - is
rigaya's work as well. This project contributes the packaging: a standalone
module with a C API, a device-in/device-out interface, the CMake build for both
platforms, and the test driver. See RtgmDif.h for what the module adds on top of
the filter itself.

If you use this project, please also consider the upstream project it is built
on; the filter's design, its presets and its parameter semantics are all
documented there.

