===============================================================================
3. Modifications relative to upstream NVEnc
===============================================================================

The MIT License only requires the copyright notice and permission text to be
kept, not a list of changes - but a reader should be able to tell at a glance
what is upstream and what is not, so the modifications are listed here. All of
them were made in September 2026, while turning the filter into a standalone
module; every other file under RtgmDif/NVEnc/ is upstream code unchanged.

Modified:

    NVEnc/NVEncCore/NVEncFilter.h
        Removed the NPPI_DLL_NAME_TSTR / NVRTC_DLL_NAME_TSTR declarations and
        check_if_nppi_dll_available(), none of which had a caller here.

    NVEnc/NVEncCore/NVEncFilter.cpp
        Removed the body of check_if_nppi_dll_available() for the same reason.

    NVEnc/NVEncCore/NVEncFilterParam.cpp
        Replaced five calls to cmd_string_to_bool() with an inline yes/no parse,
        so that this translation unit no longer needs the command line parser.

    NVEnc/NVEncCore/NVEncFilterNnedi.cu
        Made the default weights lookup (nnediDefaultWeightFilePath) and its file
        name platform-independent. Upstream only had them for Windows, so on
        Linux an empty weight path went down the "embedded resource" route and
        failed with RGY_ERR_INVALID_PARAM.

    NVEnc/NVEncCore/rgy_memmem.cpp, NVEnc/NVEncCore/rgy_bitstream.cpp
        Their CPU-feature dispatch now returns the scalar implementation
        directly; see the deleted files below.

Deleted:

    NVEnc/NVEncCore/rgy_memmem_avx2.cpp
    NVEnc/NVEncCore/rgy_memmem_avx512bw.cpp
    NVEnc/NVEncCore/rgy_bitstream_avx2.cpp
    NVEnc/NVEncCore/rgy_bitstream_avx512bw.cpp

    AVX2/AVX512BW implementations of bitstream parsing and memory searching.
    They exist to accelerate the NVEncC front end's file reading, which this
    module does not do - it receives device frames and returns device frames -
    and their entry points had no caller here. Deleting them is what removed the
    last /arch:AVX2 and /arch:AVX512 from the build.

    NVEnc/NVEncSDK/Common/inc/helper_cuda_drvapi.h
    NVEnc/NVEncSDK/Common/inc/helper_functions.h

    Two NVIDIA headers that nothing in this tree includes. Dropped so that the
    list in section 2(b) is only what the build actually needs.

Added (not upstream code, original to this project):

    NVEnc/NVEncCore/rgy_config.h
        The Linux-side platform configuration that rgy_version.h expects to
        include on non-Windows builds. Upstream carries it; the vendored subset
        did not.

    NVEnc/rtgmc_cmd_stub.cpp, NVEnc/rtgmc_linux_stubs.cpp
        Stand-ins for upstream translation units that this module does not
        vendor, so the link closes without their baggage.

    NVEnc/rtgmc_config.h
        Force-included on every translation unit to turn off the optional
        features (NVVFX, NGX, NVRTC, NVML, ONNX, libplacebo, ffmpeg ...) that a
        pure deinterlacing module does not need.

Everything outside RtgmDif/NVEnc/ - the CMake build, RtgmDif.h/.cpp, the C API,
RtgmDifTest - is original to this project.
